sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: Nick 2026-11-06, agent strip (a): a log read is a typed source of the agent's log streaming. No SSH, no agent command, no Swamp run (R1).
  %% Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06): a production Instance's log is read through a read-only group, `orbit-logs`, that the agent's unit joins. Production apps and the observer's read-only rule stay unchanged.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:logs
  %% kind: instance.logs
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane A icon=server pill=observer tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant A as Node agent<br/>orbit-agent
  CLI->>GW: instance:logs <instance>
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:logs <instance>`
  %%> - syntax: `instance:logs <instance> [--lines=COUNT] [--follow] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the numeric Instance ID from `instance:list`
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI, the web app and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, open a tail<br/>source: the Instance log
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Node that serves the Instance
  %%> - the agent of that Node has a fresh view and has joined its log channel
  %%> - the Node has a free stream slot (16 for each Node)
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Gateway opens the tail for itself with the requested line count and starts it at once; it needs no viewer channel
  %%> - the source is derived by the Gateway: `storage/logs/laravel.log` in the Instance's application directory, or the newest `laravel-*.log` when that file is absent
  %%> - the caller names no path or unit
  GW->>A: log-streams.changed
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - prompts the agent to fetch its stream list over HTTPS; the event carries no data
  Note over A: Read the newest lines<br/>log file, read-only
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the agent reads the file itself and starts no program
  %%> - a development Instance: the file under the development Instance root
  %%> - a production Instance: the shared `storage/logs` directory of the application in the production home carries a read ACL for the group `orbit-logs`, which the agent's unit joins; the unit already binds the production home back read-only
  %%> - it refuses a file that root owns and a link at `storage/logs` or at the file
  %%> - the agent redacts each line and sends the first lines as one batch, also when the batch is empty, so the Gateway knows the read is complete
  A->>GW: Lines<br/>log channel
  alt lines arrive within 5 s
    Note over GW: Redact, close the tail<br/>stored environment values
    GW-->>CLI: 200 lines<br/>truncated flag
    %%> Result:
    %%> - at most the requested number of newest lines and 256 KiB; `truncated` is set when either limit left out older lines
    %%> - an Instance without a log file is an empty list
  else agent cannot answer
    Note over GW: Close the tail<br/>frees the stream slot
    GW--xCLI: 409 logs.live_unavailable<br/>reason
    %%> When:
    %%> - the agent view is stale, the agent has not joined its log channel, the source cannot be read, or no batch arrives within 5 s
    %%> - `logs.stream_limit` (429) when the Node already has 16 open tails
    %%> Result:
    %%> - there is no SSH fallback and no polling; read again once the agent is back
  end
